w: I greet Thee, who my sure Re- deem- er art, My on- ly trust and Sa- vior of my heart,
w: Thou art the King of mer- cy and of grace, Reig- ning om- ni- po- tent in ev- ery place;
w: Thou art the life, by which a- lone we live, And all our sub- stance and our strength re- ceive;
w: Thou hast the true and per- fect gen- tle- ness, No harsh- ness hast Thou and no bit- ter- ness;
w: Our hope is in no oth- er save in Thee; Our faith is built up- on Thy pro- mise free;
c2 c B | A2 G2 | A c c =B | c4 | A2 G F | E F G B | A2 G2 | F4 |]
w: Who pain didst un- der- go for my poor sake; I pray Thee from our hearts all cares to take.
w: So come, O King, and our whole be- ing sway; Shine on us with the light of Thy pure day.
w: Sustain us by Thy faith and by Thy pow- er, And give us strength in ev- ery try- ing hour.
w: O grant to us the grace we find in Thee, That we may dwell in per- fect u- ni- ty.
w: Lord, give us peace, and make us calm and sure, That in Thy strength we ev- er- more en- dure.
